<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50083" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae</span></b> , interj.
		
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐαί</span>
		, an exclamation of pain or dread, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>ah! alas!</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(a).</b>
			<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Mantua, vae, miserae nimium vicina Cremonae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Verg.
					E. 9, 28</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Hor. C. 1, 13, 3</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae verbero!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Mil. 2, 3, 51</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(b).</b>
			Very freq. like the Gr. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐαί</span> and
			our <i>woe!</i> with <i>dat.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae misero mihi!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 2, 2, 94</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Ter. Heaut. 2, 3, 9</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mihi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Eun. 4, 4, 42</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">illi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut.
					As. 2, 2, 7</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tergo meo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Men. 2, 2, 3</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">id. Capt. 3, 4, 117</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">capiti atque aetati tuae,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					Rud. 2, 3, 44</span></i>
			.—Esp., in the exclamation ascribed to Brennus: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae victis! intoleranda Romanis vox,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Liv.
					5, 48, 9</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Flor. 1, 13, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Fest. p.
				372</span></i> Müll.; <i><span class="en">Plaut. Ps.
				5, 2, 19</span></i>; also, as title of a Satire by Varro, v.
					<i><span class="en">Non. 82, 17</span></i>; <i><span class="en">156,
			13</span></i>; <i><span class="en">492, 8</span></i> (Müll. de
			victis).— </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense5"><b>(g).</b>
			Very rarely with <i>acc.</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae te!</span>”
				
					<i>woe to you!</i>
				
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. As. 2, 4, 75</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">scelesta, vae te!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cat. 8,
					15</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vae me!</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Sen. Apocol. 4, 3</span></i>
			. </div>
